1
00:00:00,100 --> 00:00:02,500
This diner's fridge is a polar bear. It doesn't open easily.

2
00:00:02,700 --> 00:00:05,100
A little earlier, in the alley. Mochi's nose was following the smoke.

3
00:00:05,300 --> 00:00:07,700
Next door, long lines. Here, no one.

4
00:00:07,900 --> 00:00:12,500
The owner is Mu, a cat chef. Grilling alone again today.

5
00:00:12,700 --> 00:00:15,100
First customers. Mu is surprised. Only his ear shows it.

6
00:00:15,300 --> 00:00:19,900
Today's grilled fish. The color is a bit... deep.

7
00:00:20,100 --> 00:00:22,500
There is a reason this place is empty.

8
00:00:22,700 --> 00:00:25,100
The fridge won't hand over the fish. Even asleep.

9
00:00:25,300 --> 00:00:27,700
So Mu grills whatever he can grab.

10
00:00:27,900 --> 00:00:32,500
Mochi's nose can't find the way home. It can find the right fish.

11
00:00:32,700 --> 00:00:35,100
Mu's eyes opened. A first since opening day.

12
00:00:35,300 --> 00:00:37,500
Mochi was hired on the spot.

13
00:00:37,700 --> 00:00:40,100
Kong helps too. Cheek pouches are not allowed.

14
00:00:40,300 --> 00:00:42,700
A good smell doesn't wait in line.

15
00:00:42,900 --> 00:00:45,300
That night, not a single empty seat. Mr. Giraffe used the window.

16
00:00:45,500 --> 00:00:47,900
Mu did not smile. His tail did it for him.

17
00:00:48,100 --> 00:00:52,500
Even the fridge opened by itself.

18
00:00:52,700 --> 00:00:55,100
Mu doesn't talk. He wrapped fish instead.

19
00:00:55,300 --> 00:00:59,700
Kong asked: where does this parcel go?

20
00:00:59,900 --> 00:01:02,700
Train, lighthouse, ship, iceberg. The last ship leaves after three sunrises.

21
00:01:02,900 --> 00:01:05,300
Three days. One lost penguin, one late courier.

22
00:01:05,500 --> 00:01:09,300
Trains don't wait. (To be continued)

